 to contact me.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nDoctor\n\n                                     Report\n Word length                  180\n Comments                     The letter summarises all important case notes\n                              in relevant paragraphs. There are only a few\n                              grammatical errors. However, some spelling\n                              errors are visible. Overall, the letter meets the\n                              expectations.\n Estimated Grade              B\n Advice                       1. Revise grammar.\n                              2. Be careful with spelling.\n                              3. Always proofread the letter after finishing it.\n Helpful links                https://www.benchmarkedu.com.au/oet-reading-\n                              practice-tests\n                              https://www.benchmarkedu.com.au/oet-writing-\n                              correction\n                              https://www.facebook.com/groups/oethelp\n\n\n\n\n296 Henley Beach Rd, Underdale, 5032\nhttp://www.benchmarkedu.com.au/oet-writing-correction\nwww.benchmarkedu.com.au/pteoetielts", "pages": [{"number": 1, "text": "Ticket Id: 26995\n\nDr. Elvira Sterinberg\nGynecologist\n123 church steet\nRichmond 3212\n\n02-02-2007\n\n\nDear Dr. Sterinberg,\n\nRE: Mrs. Larissa Zaneeta\n\nThank you for seeing Mrs Zaneeta whose features are suggestive of secondary infertility.\n\nMrs Zaneeta is a 38- year-old marketing manker. She is married and has only a 4-year-old boy.                Comment [teacher1]: manager\n\nOn 11/07/2005, she presented with stress related anexity and sleeping disorder. She was on oral              Comment [teacher2]: anxiety\ncontraceptive pills then stopped contraception in April 2006. Four months following cessation of             Comment [teacher3]: which she\n                                                                                                             stopped later\ncontraception, 